findings.notes:
The execution matches the approved plan:
- the model-free diagnostic (T and E) was created before any training;
- the sweep {1e-4, 3e-4, 1e-3} at seed 17 ran for both arms, before the confirmation runs;
- fresh seeds 101/202/303 ran at each arm's own selected LR;
- every run ended at tokens_seen 2,000,000,000 and step 244,160, using the README command form;
- one set of code and data hashes covers all runs;
- evaluation used only the three held-out sources, with 172,032 targets.
Deviations are disclosed and explained: parallel execution on identical cards; the three B sweep 2B checkpoints not retained (hashes and per-target arrays kept; S4 not triggered, so no decision depended on them); the unconditional, symmetric rescore kept outside the decision chain, with its output embedded per run rather than in a separate rescore-floor.json; and two failed pre-provisioning submissions. No crashes, NaNs, restarts or extra runs.
